   The partner set is CONTAINED in {p1 = 1} below and on the line, and in the
   two 2-faces (p2,p3) in {(0,1),(1,0)} above it -- that is item 2's efficiency
   closed form, used as given -- so these boxes pin the dimension at EXACTLY 3
   below and on the line and EXACTLY 2 above it, at every game tested.

   SATURATION.  Predicted: every efficient strategy is a partner exactly on
   {u <= 1, v <= 0} below/on the line, and -- for the live (0,1) sheet -- on
   {u >= 0, v >= 0} above it.  Per-game agreement:
      22 of 22 games agree; disagreements: none
      and saturation of the WHOLE efficient set above the line (both sheets)
      needs T = S as well: 9 of 9 above-line games agree; disagreements: none

